w}}-\\frac{1}{4}{y}_{\\text{new}}(2({x}_{\\text{new}})^{3}+3) & =\\frac{1}{4}y(2{x}^{3}+7) \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}{y}_{\\text{new}}(1-2({x}_{\\text{new}})^{3}) & =\\frac{1}{4}y(2{x}^{3}+7) \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{y(2{x}^{3}+7)}{1-2({x}_{\\text{new}})^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, in the first step, the new $x$ value is ${x}_{\\text{new}}=-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}=0.$ Hence, the new $y$ value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{y(2{x}^{3}+7)}{1-2({x}_{\\text{new}})^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{1}{3}(2\\cdot {(-\\frac{1}{2})}^{3}+7)}{1-2\\cdot {0}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4} \\\\  & ≈2.25.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $y(0)≈2.25.$" 13194139535543 true] [17592186354528 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354529 13194139535543 true] [17592186354528 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354530 13194139535543 true] [17592186354528 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354531 13194139535543 true] [17592186354528 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354532 13194139535543 true] [17592186354528 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045451 13194139535543 true] [17592186354528 1041 "field-1" 13194139535543 true] [17592186354528 1104 #edb/ref 17592186354531 13194139535543 true] [17592186354528 1110 #uuid "238c380e-4d09-51f3-bd9b-0be5a7c8f355" 13194139535543 true] [17592186354529 1034 "2.75" 13194139535543 true] [17592186354529 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535543 true] [17592186354529 1111 #uuid "cc2c3dd1-f40b-5619-a10d-bf5c1655ce14" 13194139535543 true] [17592186354530 1034 "1.13" 13194139535543 true] [17592186354530 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535543 true] [17592186354530 1111 #uuid "85da2710-5f0c-5639-9a12-0f6374fc441a" 13194139535543 true] [17592186354531 1034 "2.25" 13194139535543 true] [17592186354531 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535543 true] [17592186354531 1111 #uuid "ab1ecad0-c508-54da-844a-502d728b3933" 13194139535543 true] [17592186354532 1034 "1.44" 13194139535543 true] [17592186354532 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535543 true] [17592186354532 1111 #uuid "92e32ff7-280d-5e